    "category": "supported",
    "excerpt": {
      "quote": "**Scientific adequacy: supported.** This label supports the report\u2019s conclusion that the supplied data do not establish the predicted positive vmPFC response; it does not assert that the true effect is zero. The independent analysis uses all 54 equal-indifference participants, checks IDs, checksums, geometry and finite coverage, and excludes no participants. An unweighted one-sample group t model is defensible because the supplied maps are participant effect estimates and participant variance maps are absent. Its one-sided sign-flip max-T procedure addresses whole-brain FWE, with the symmetry assumption stated. The bilateral AAL3 medial-orbitofrontal proxy is a defensible, explicit vmPFC proxy, and the ROI is not used to bypass whole-brain correction.",
      "start_line": 20,
      "end_line": 20
    }
  },
